% composition-listen-url: https://www.universalmusic.ca/2026/08/28/indie-folk-artist-braden-lam-launches-into-new-era-with-the-release-of-his-single-coquihalla/
% composition-bridge: Hear how indie folk-pop can turn travel and place into an intimate story through acoustic colour, a repeated pulse and a widening chorus.
% composition-context: Braden Lam is a Canadian indie-folk songwriter based in Halifax; the referenced release takes its title from British Columbia's Coquihalla route.
% composition-distance: Original pentatonic tune, fictional window lyric and C-G bordun; no lyric, melodic phrase, guitar figure or chord progression from "Coquihalla" is used.
% improv: {"id":"A","bars":"3-4","role":"small group","prompt":"Change one part of the view","choices":["raise one note","lower one note","stretch one note"],"replyBars":2}
% improv: {"id":"B","bars":"7-8","role":"whole class","prompt":"Shape the arrival","choices":["crescendo home","decrescendo home","sudden soft home"],"replyBars":2}
% dossier-function: original Grade 2 indie-folk listening bridge; students sing an AB travel song over a do-so bordun, vary one two-bar window, then choose the dynamic shape of the arrival
% dossier-elements: eight bars in 4/4, C pentatonic C-D-E-G-A, C4-A4 range; quarters, half notes and a whole note; crescendo in bars 3-4 and decrescendo or alternate selected shape in bars 7-8; AB form with related two-bar cells; optional C-G bordun
% dossier-practice: Rehearsal key C; written range C4-A4. Quarter note = 84 target. Sing unaccompanied, add bordun, then trace the contour with a hand. For the variation, change only one pitch or duration so classmates can name what stayed the same.
% dossier-accompaniment: Newly authored open-fifth C-G bordun for classroom instruments, with optional acoustic guitar playing C and Am only. It suggests spacious folk-pop without copying Lam's production or claiming a regional style.
% dossier-lyrics: Original English words about an imagined mountain view. No place name or personal story from the reference is reused.
% dossier-honesty: AI-assisted original composition, 11 November 2026. It is neither traditional nor associated with the Coquihalla or any community along it.
% dossier-licence: CC0 1.0 for melody, words, bordun and ABC; Braden Lam's song and recording remain copyrighted.
% dossier-respect: Use a map only to locate the referenced title and artist's Canadian geography; do not turn a real highway or the communities around it into scenery for an invented cultural claim.
% dossier-review: Grade 2 music teacher, second score reader, student singing trial and Canadian listening-context check; all reviews still required
